hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16756","He said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from a woman among them, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was eating with my left, and I was a left-handed woman, and he struck my hand and the morsel fell; he said: Do not eat with your left when Allah, blessed and exalted, has made for you a right, or he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has freed your right for you; he said: So my left turned into a right, and I did not eat with it afterward."
"16767","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Damra ibn Said, from his grandmother, from a woman of their women, he said: and she had prayed the two qiblas with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said to me: Dye, one of you leaves dye until her hand is like the hand of a man; she said: So she did not leave dye until she met Allah, mighty and majestic, though she would dye though she was eighty."
